WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.230
Daisuke!

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:03.350
Jinko!

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.850
<b>The Regular Meet Thus Far</b>

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.070
The regular meet thus far!

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.140
The second round was on fire!

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.970
Shiki-kun got paired up with Sonohara 
Akira-kun from Sekigawata Middle School,

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.330
and they stormed through to Round 3!

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.360
Not bad, considering he's Koshiyama!

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:20.490
But his partner, Akira-kun, seemed
a handful in so many ways...

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:25.000
Plus, we realized he was the guy 
we saw in Akiba dressed as a girl!

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.000
<b>Round 3</b>

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.000
We don't wanna miss Round 3, no way!

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.840
<b>Question 10: "The Unparalleled Super Ace"</b>

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:01.930
I'm sorry for the way he behaved in Round 2.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.390
No, I should apologize for the trouble 
my foolish brother has caused.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:08.390
We'd like you to refrain from such 
combative behavior from now on.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:09.830
Is that a challenge?

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:10.900
Sonohara!

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.300
He's one energetic middle 
schooler, isn't he?

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:17.110
What's the problem, anyway? 
He didn't break any rules.

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:19.860
I kinda like that play style.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.600
It's true that he didn't 
break any rules, but...

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:23.440
Yeah.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.540
This is Kannami's club president, 
Hanabusa-san, a third-year,

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.330
and Shibuya-san, who's also a third-year.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:32.630
They're Kannami's top two students and 
place high in the meet every year.

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:35.470
My club's members are <i>very</i> 
particular about etiquette.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:39.380
The next time he takes things 
too far, we will make a complaint.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:42.390
I see you Leoneil guys 
are as uptight as ever!

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.390
We just want to take this contest seriously.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:49.710
Yokohama's Kannami and Chiba's Leoneil 
have always shared an intense rivalry.

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.100
Oh...

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:54.110
All of you lack discipline.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.980
Whether that novice participates or not,

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.940
he's no match for Kaijou.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:03.070
<i>The guys from Kaijou somehow 
seem really intimidating...</i>

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:06.590
Boy, you guys have a presence 
like no other team here.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.530
Of the 18 players in Round 3,

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.040
six are from Kaijou.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.720
Hmph. You reek of old man stench.

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:12.790
<b>Are you really
 second-years?</b>

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:12.790
Are you really second-years?

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.040
Come on, not again!

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.750
That's enough baiting one another.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.800
Settle this fair and square 
through quiz bowl.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.760
We will now announce the groups for Round 3.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.310
Winner

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.310
<b>Final</b>

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.650
<b>Asagaoka Regular Meet</b>

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.650
<b>Stage Progression</b>

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.870
The 18 participants in 
Round 3 have been divided

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:37.190
impartially into groups based 
on your paper quiz results.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.360
<b>Semifinal</b>

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.190
<b>Konoe | Tozuka | Hanabusa | Hosokawa | Kumada | Kawabata | Fukami | Yagi
Ohkura | Ashiya | Shibuya | Shibata | Mikuriya | Koizumi | Koshiyama | Sonohara | Hirosue</b>

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.190
<b>3R Quarterfinal</b>

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.750
We'll start with the first group,

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:42.950
so if you're in the second group, you 
can sit in the audience for now.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:47.410
It may be impartial, but those are 
both pretty brutal groupings...

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:48.620
Sasajima.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:52.730
Obviously, we'll be in separate groups,
 since we placed first and second.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.540
I'll be waiting for you in the semifinal.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.510
You're in the second group, aren't you?

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:58.130
So he'll be the one waiting.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.090
Yeah. I look forward to it.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:04.300
Wow...

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.260
This should be fun, huh?

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.850
You won't be able to do a thing.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.230
You're not a quiz freak, after all.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:20.440
Good luck in the first group!

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.410
Koshiyama.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:24.240
Yes?

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.200
Watch closely.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:30.790
The time has come.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:36.130
Round 3, "All Who Draw the Sword Will 
Die by the Sword," will now begin.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.130
<b>Round 3</b>

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.130
<b>"All Who Draw the Sword Will 
Die by the Sword" Multiple Answers 
Quiz and Fastest Finger Board Quiz</b>

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:39.680
Participants in the first 
group, please step up here.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:45.970
From left to right, we have:

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:48.410
Buzou High School 
second-year, Sasajima-kun.

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:52.350
He beat out the prestigious Kaijou Academy 
with the top score on the paper quiz.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:58.480
<i>Sasajima, I still remember the day 
you joined our club very clearly.</i>

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:03.370
<i>Last spring, when Kaijou's quiz team was
 lauded as the champions of the east,</i>

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:06.710
<i>and the club's morale was starting to slip,</i>

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:09.490
<i>you blew in like the wind.</i>

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:10.740
Perfect numbers.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:12.070
Correct.

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:13.500
Question.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.870
Japan's only desert, the Ura-sabaku, is—

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.080
Tokyo.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.590
<b>Q: Japan's only desert, the Ura-sabaku, 
is in which prefecture? A: Tokyo</b>

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:20.590
Correct.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:24.510
<i>Ohkura's being totally 
out-buzzed by the rookie...</i>

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:26.710
Don't you guys want to join in?

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.340
Ah, no, we'll pass.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.050
President, I brought him.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:32.460
Please don't waste my time.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.770
I still have student council work to do.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.510
Hey, don't be like that.

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:39.960
You can find time to meet 
our newest member, can't you?

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:40.770
Question.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.610
With the atomic number 107, and sym—

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.130
Bohrium.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:45.940
Correct.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:47.450
<b>Q: With the atomic number 107, and symbol Bh, which transuranium element is named after Danish physicist 
Niels Bohr, who won the Nobel Prize for Physics in 1922?  A: Bohrium</b>

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:47.450
Who's he?

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:49.920
Sasajima Gakuto, a first-year.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:51.520
He only started here in high school,

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.410
after coming in from a 
different middle school.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.710
He obviously has some 
experience of quizzing.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:57.970
Question.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.920
"With great power comes great 
responsibility" is the lesson—

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:05.100
Sword of Damocles.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:05.880
<b>Q: "With great power comes great responsibility" is the lesson 
King Dionysus of Syracuse taught his retainer, Damocles, in what 
famous parable? A: Sword of Damocles</b>

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:05.880
Correct.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.390
Hey, Fukami joined in!

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:10.510
I haven't seen him press a buzzer in ages!

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:15.220
<i>The two of you were perfectly matched.</i>

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.190
<i>From then on, you demonstrated 
your true abilities,</i>

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:21.900
<i>and produced stellar results 
in a number of meets.</i>

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:25.280
And from Group A in Round 
2, we have this duo:

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:28.120
Buzou High School first-year Fukami-san...

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.090
Good luck!

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.440
Yeah, you too!

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.160
...and Kannami High School 
first-year Yagi-san.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:34.370
So after workin' together as a 
pair, now they're facin' off...

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.620
They're still so friendly, though.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:40.080
These are the nine participants 
in the first group of Round 3.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.380
I will now explain the rules.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:47.430
Round 3 will combine the total scores

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:52.180
of a multiple answers quiz and a fastest 
finger board quiz with 20 questions.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:56.060
You'll earn points toward your initial 
score for each correct answer

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:59.430
in the multiple answers portion, but if 
even one of your answers is incorrect,

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:00.440
you get zero points.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.310
Man, that's strict!

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:03.690
So it's a bad idea to go all out.

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:08.900
We'll begin Round 3 with the multiple 
answers quiz to determine your initial scores.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:11.110
You'll have 60 seconds to 
think about your answers.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.650
Question.

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:15.910
Leonardo da Vinci's famous 
painting is <i>The Last Supper</i>.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:19.540
List the names of the twelve apostles 
depicted in this painting.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:22.250
<b>Apostles.......?</b>

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:22.250
"Apostles?"

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:25.210
<i>Should've known they'd
use a question like this.</i>

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:26.570
You know this one?

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:28.390
It's a famous painting,

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:30.790
and those twelve people 
are fairly well-known.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:33.840
I don't understand by what standards 
you consider that "well-known."

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:38.580
The painting illustrates 
the moment that Christ

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:42.060
tells his twelve apostles that 
one of them will betray him.

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:45.190
<i>The first one that springs to 
mind is the traitor, Judas.</i>

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:48.240
<i>The twelve apostles showed up in the 
Christianity-related questions</i>

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:51.250
<i>Sasajima-senpai came up with 
to prepare us for this meet.</i>

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:54.280
Time's up.

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:57.620
Let's see your answers. 
Reveal your boards!

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:05.380
Michael 
Gabriel 
Raphael 
Uriel

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:00.040
Oh, too bad!

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.330
Those are angels, not apostles.

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:05.380
Aw, I should've known...

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:07.550
Next: Fukami-san.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.500
Judas 
Peter 
James

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:08.690
Five points!

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.380
<i>I did it, Sasajima-senpai!</i>

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.130
Judas

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:14.750
Kawabata-kun gets one point.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.510
Judas 
James

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:16.550
Kumada-kun, two points.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:20.580
Hosokawa-kun, unfortunately, has two 
wrong answers, so that's zero points.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:21.310
Judas
Matthew

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:21.310
Mark 
John
Luke

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:21.310
You're kidding!

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:24.070
Hanabusa-kun, painfully, 
also earns zero points!

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:25.520
Judas
Luke
Mark
James

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:25.520
Matthew
John
Peter 
Paul

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.520
Don't say "painfully"!

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.980
Judas
Matthew
John
Simon

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.980
James (Son of Alphaeus)
James (Son of Zebedee)
Peter
Philip

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.440
Tozuka-kun, well done! Eight points!

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:32.950
Judas Iscariot
Thaddeus
Matthew

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:32.950
Konoe-kun earns six points, 
and Sasajima-kun...

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.910
<b>Bartholomew
James (Son of Alphaeus)
James (Son of Zebedee)
Andrew
Judas Iscariot
Peter</b>

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.910
<b>John
Thomas
Philip
Matthew
Thaddeus
Simon</b>

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.910
Excellent! A perfect answer!

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:39.160
He earns twelve points!

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.710
Sasajima-senpai!

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.580
Your team president's amazing.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:44.460
Total

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:44.460
Multiple
Answers

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:48.040
Now, you will enter the fastest finger 
board quiz with these initial scores.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.040
Sasajima | Konoe | Tozuka | Hanabusa | Hosokawa | Kumada | Kawabata | Fukami | Yagi

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:50.910
The crucial bit of the fastest 
finger board quiz is that...

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.700
...buzzing in with a correct 
answer earns you three points.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:58.050
Answer incorrectly, and 
you lose three points.

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:02.190
Answering correctly without 
buzzing earns you one point.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:05.890
An incorrect answer will 
not change your score.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:11.330
Also, being the only player to answer 
correctly is worth a bonus point, right?

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:15.230
Yes. And the following is at 
the core of this round's rules:

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:16.990
If you buzz in and answer correctly,

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.530
you earn the right to alter the 
points earned by the other players.

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:22.660
Alter their points?

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:26.580
All three, or even four, of the points 
you earn for a correct answer

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:31.270
can be added to your own score or subtracted 
from another player's score at your discretion.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:33.860
So you can add them all to 
your own score if you want?

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:34.960
Of course.

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:41.390
You can also keep two points for yourself 
and subtract one from another player.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.270
Total

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.270
Multiple
Answers

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:44.280
The first player to 20 points wins.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:51.610
Sasajima | Konoe | Tozuka | Hanabusa | Hosokawa | Kumada | Kawabata | Fukami | Yagi

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:48.100
If your score enters negative 
numbers, you are disqualified.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:51.610
Three players from each group 
will advance to the semifinal.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:57.240
What happens if we don't have three 
winners at the end of 20 questions?

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.400
The players with the highest scores 
will be declared the winners.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:03.240
If there's a tie, we'll enter sudden death.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:07.210
<i>How they choose to distribute their 
own points will be crucial, for sure.</i>

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:10.170
The fastest finger board 
quiz will now begin.

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:11.570
Question.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:15.240
On this day, June 3, in 1950, Herzog—

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:18.380
The first to buzz was...

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.350
Oh, it was me?

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:24.980
<i>Sasajima-senpai </i>did<i> say he always 
keeps a buzzer in his pocket,</i>

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:26.730
<i>but he buzzes from the hip during meets, too?</i>

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:29.760
Players, please write down your answer.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.160
You'll have 15 seconds to think.

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:35.940
<i>Another date-based question... 
I'm glad I didn't buzz in.</i>

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.320
Show your boards.

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:40.700
The correct answer is Annapurna.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:41.740
<b>Annapurna</b>

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:43.700
<b>Q: On this day, June 3, in 1950, Herzog led a French mountaineering 
expedition to reach the peak of which 8,000-meter-tall mountain?  A. Annapurna</b>

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.700
Sasajima-kun, since you buzzed 
in and answered correctly,

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:46.100
you can distribute your 
three points as you like.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:48.660
I'll keep them all.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:50.040
<b>Sasajima</b>

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:50.040
<b>Total</b>

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:53.210
Wow, he didn't subtract any from anyone.

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:56.460
He could've plunged some of those guys into 
negative figures and got them disqualified.

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:58.950
You just don't get it, do you?

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:01.980
Competitors with scores that far below 
his aren't even worth worrying about.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:05.390
Rather than taking others out, 
he chose to win it quickly.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:08.600
If he buzzes in and answers 
right two more times, he wins!

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:12.150
Once again, the first to 
buzz was Sasajima-kun.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:18.360
Ice cream headache

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:15.790
The correct answer gives him three points.

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:18.360
I'll keep them all.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.700
<b>Sasajima</b>

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.700
<b>Total</b>

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:23.160
Sasajima-kun buzzes in for 
the third time in a row!

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:26.120
Church of the 
Holy Cross

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:26.120
Correct! He earns three points!

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:27.180
That was fast!

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:28.940
That gives him 20 points!

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:33.340
Konoe-senpai's usually more 
aggressive on the buzzer.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:36.830
Trying specifically to beat Sasajima 
to the buzzer would be the same

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:39.050
as buzzing reflexively, and likely 
to result in a wrong answer.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:44.020
When up against someone you know 
is at a higher level than you,

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:47.930
sometimes, it's wisest to let them win first.

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:51.890
<i>What's important is to 
end up in the top three.</i>

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:52.520
Total

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:52.520
Multiple
Answers

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:55.480
Sasajima-kun, how will you 
distribute your points?

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.480
Sasajima | Konoe | Tozuka | Hanabusa | Hosokawa | Kumada | Kawabata | Fukami | Yagi

00:11:55.770 --> 00:12:00.740
With three points, couldn't he just keep 
them, smash the 20-point barrier, and win?

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:02.230
He sure could.

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:05.660
He has one point left over.

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:08.340
I see.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.920
So the person who buzzes in and 
answers correctly has the right

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:13.620
to use his points effectively, 
to the very last one, yes?

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:16.090
Exactly.

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:19.590
Does that mean he's forced to 
subtract a point from someone?

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:21.500
That's brutal...

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.320
He's already won.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:25.950
What do the other guys' scores matter?

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:30.470
No, he said "to use them effectively."

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:33.690
The way he chooses to subtract 
a point will be significant.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.900
<i>Getting a point taken away 
by Sasajima now means...</i>

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:39.530
<i>...he could stop a specific 
person from going through!</i>

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:42.780
<i>It'll be someone he doesn't want 
to face in the next round.</i>

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:46.160
<i>In other words, someone he 
acknowledges as being a threat.</i>

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:50.660
Then, I'll take a point from 
Tozuka-san of Leoneil.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.080
Total

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.080
Multiple
Answers

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.080
Sasajima | Konoe | Tozuka | Hanabusa

00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:55.290
Well, I can't fault you for that.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:13:01.300
<b>Sasajima</b>

00:12:55.290 --> 00:13:01.300
<b>Total</b>

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:58.750
Sasajima-kun has reached 20 points,

00:12:58.750 --> 00:12:59.980
finishing in first place!

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.300
Congratulations!

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:03.550
Way to go, ex-Kaijou kid!

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.220
<b>I can't see...</b>

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.160
So it's true, then?

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:21.530
I wasn't certain before, but now...

00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:25.490
Yep. He's the Sasajima Gakuto who 
was in our club up until last year.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:24.480
He used to go to Kaijou?

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:27.230
He's the Sasajima that went to Kaijou?

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.490
The unparalleled super ace.

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:29.950
<i>"Super ace"?</i>

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.910
Did he really have to say that?

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:35.120
Huh? Did I say something I shouldn't have?

00:13:35.650 --> 00:13:37.580
Silence, please. The 
competition is still ongoing.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:41.330
I am now Sasajima of Buzou.

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:48.550
I'll continue with the questions.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:52.200
<i>Sasajima-senpai went to Kaijou?</i>

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:54.390
<i>The super ace of the quiz team?</i>

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:57.480
Quiz bowl is pointless.

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:01.890
Fukami-san...

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:03.440
Please show your board.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:05.730
Oh... Sorry.

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:09.230
<i>I didn't even hear the question.</i>

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:12.340
Sasajima-senpai, is it true?

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:15.450
That you were on Kaijou's quiz team?

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:19.170
Yes, I was. But only for six months.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:22.960
But you still left your mark 
on the Kaijou quiz bowl team.

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:25.840
You hadn't told the members of your new club?

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:29.550
There was no opportunity, 
nor any need, to bring it up.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.210
<i>There wasn't?</i>

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:34.030
<i>The topic of Kaijou did come up a few times.</i>

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:36.930
<i>It wouldn't have seemed 
out of place to tell us then.</i>

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:40.270
<i>What now? I can't concentrate...</i>

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:44.010
That Fukami girl... Is she Fukami Seiji's...

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:44.900
It seems so.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.860
So you do know Fukami-san's brother?

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:51.820
Fukami and Sasajima 
were the best of rivals.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:53.030
Huh?!

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.370
They competed against each other every day

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.040
to polish their skills in a battle 
to be Kaijou's star player.

00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:02.380
The atmosphere when they faced 
each other was always volatile.

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:06.180
Stop making it sound so dramatic, Ohkura.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:07.970
No, let me say it, Sasajima!

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:10.400
The day you joined our club

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:13.430
and you two faced off 
on the buzzers, I knew.

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:16.140
I knew you two would carry 
Kaijou's quiz team...

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:19.330
No, the entire world of 
high school quiz bowl.

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:22.260
But six months later,

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:27.240
something happened between you 
that only the two of you know about.

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:32.410
Then, you left Kaijou, and Fukami 
quit quiz bowl altogether.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:35.370
What the heck happened?

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:39.500
Nothing, really.

00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:42.250
All right! 20 points on the nose!

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.250
Human
Beatbox

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:46.040
Hanabusa-kun of Kannami University 
High School goes through.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:46.920
Total

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:46.920
Multiple
Answers

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:49.170
Only one more player can join the winners.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.170
Sasajima | Konoe | Tozuka | Hanabusa | Hosokawa | Kumada | Kawabata | Fukami | Yagi

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:58.390
<i>Do those two know the real reason 
my brother quit quiz bowl?</i>

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:03.250
<i>Being a part of quiz bowl has 
never felt like such a burden...</i>

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:06.090
Fukami-san, look up!

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:08.150
Focus on the match!

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:09.530
Listen to the questions!

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:11.530
Damn straight! You're just gettin' started!

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:21.040
Question.

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:23.580
Hebrew for "God heal—

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:26.290
<i>It lit up!</i>

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.000
Can she get it from just that?

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:32.470
Yeah. We know this one.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.930
<i>I buzzed almost reflexively, but...</i>

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:38.880
The questions Sasajima-senpai 
put together to prepare us

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:42.060
for this meet involved a 
lot of Christian topics.

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:43.770
Show your boards.

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:44.190
<b>Messiah</b>

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:44.770
<b>Messiah</b>

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:46.480
The correct answer is Raphael.

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:46.480
<b>Gabriel</b>

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:50.070
Gabriel

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:50.070
Raphael

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:50.070
Manna

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:49.560
Fukami-san is the only 
one to answer correctly!

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:53.780
<b>Q: Hebrew for "God heals," the Christian patron of travelers 
and the ailing, one of three Archangels along with Michael and Gabriel, 
was known by what name?  A: Raphael</b>

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:53.780
That gives you a bonus point, 
for a total of four points.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.240
<i>I did it!</i>

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:57.200
She did it!

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:03.280
<i>I'm curious about my brother's past,</i>

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.800
<i>but that has nothing to do 
with my own quiz bowl career!</i>

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.340
<i>This is my first regular meet,</i>

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:12.120
<i>and I'm up against so many players.</i>

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:14.770
<i>A lot of them are really good.</i>

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:18.840
<i>There have been questions 
I've never heard before, too.</i>

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:22.310
Fukami-san, how will you 
distribute your points?

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:25.940
<i>This is all a waste if I don't enjoy it.</i>

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.150
I'll keep two for myself,

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:32.820
and subtract one each from 
Konoe-san and Tozuka-san.

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:33.820
What?!

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:35.450
She subtracted points!

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:38.420
She took points from the 
two who were on the verge

00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:41.260
of making it to the next round if they 
scored three points on the next question.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:40.740
Total

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:40.740
Multiple
Answers

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:41.910
Sasajima | Konoe | Tozuka | Hanabusa | Hosokawa | Kumada | Kawabata | Fukami | Yagi

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:44.250
Fukami-san hasn't given up yet!

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:47.920
<i>Maririn...</i>

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:49.090
Question.

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.450
Of the 88 constellations in the night sky,

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:55.510
the one that covers the 
<i>largest </i>area is Hydra, and—

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:56.800
<i>He beat me to it...</i>

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:59.110
<i>This one's a parallel question,</i>

00:17:59.110 --> 00:18:00.760
<i>and "largest" was emphasized in the reading.</i>

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.890
<b>Crux</b>

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:03.270
Show your boards.

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:07.440
Scorpio

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:07.440
Virgo

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:07.440
Crux

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:07.100
The correct answer is Crux.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:08.440
<b>Q: The one that covers the largest area is Hydra, and 
the one that covers the smallest area is what?  A: Crux</b>

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:08.440
Well done!

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:09.940
<b>Fukami</b>

00:18:09.260 --> 00:18:09.940
Question.

00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:13.990
Continents of the world: 
The "cradle of humankind"—

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:18.070
<i>"The cradle of humankind..."</i>

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:19.430
<i>Humanity's roots...</i>

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:21.750
<i>I don't know the answer,</i>

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:23.910
<i>but if it's one of the seven continents...</i>

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:26.250
Show your boards.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:28.040
<b>Africa</b>

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.040
The correct answer is Africa.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:29.000
<b>Q: Continents of the world: The "cradle of humankind"
 is a nickname for which continent?  A: Africa</b>

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:32.710
A nickname, huh?

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:34.170
<b>Fukami</b>

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:35.290
Question.

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:38.040
When an umpire has difficulty making a call,

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:39.430
he covers his eyes with both hands—

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:41.640
Yes!

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:43.890
<i>Why is she suddenly...</i>

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:46.960
Show your boards.

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:50.350
<b>Badminton</b>

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:50.350
Correct. Fukami-san earns three points.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:50.350
<b>Q: When an umpire has difficulty making a call, he covers his eyes with both
 hands in a signal meaning "I couldn't see what happened," a trademark 
of what sport in which players hit a shuttlecock to each other?  A: Badminton</b>

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:51.560
<b>Fukami</b>

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:03.790
The final player to win from 
the first group in Round 3 is...

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:10.000
Total

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:10.000
Multiple
Answers

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:10.000
Sasajima | Konoe | Tozuka | Hanabusa | Hosokawa | Kumada

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:06.040
Konoe-kun!

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:10.460
With those three points, he reclaims the 
lead from Tozuka-kun and goes through!

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:11.230
Yes!

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:23.250
Come to think of it, there was a time

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:26.970
when a girl took part in the 
Kaijou Festival quiz meet.

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:31.070
She said she started quiz bowl 
because of her older brother.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:35.520
That was before you came to Kaijou.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:39.060
Congrats, Marippe! You did great!

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:41.630
That rally toward the end was incredible!

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:43.000
You almost had it.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:43.780
Yeah.

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:46.660
I lost, though.

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:48.620
Ba-dum!

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.540
You damn normies!

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:59.020
We will now move on to the 
second group in Round 3.

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:01.010
Participants, please take to the stage.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:03.390
Finally...

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:06.470
I was getting sick of waiting.

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:08.180
<i>It's time.</i>

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:10.000
Good luck, Koshiyama!

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.250
Go get 'em!

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:11.880
Yeah.

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:16.670
<i>It's finally time, huh, Koshiyama-kun?</i>

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:20.770
<i>If we weren't at Asagaoka,</i>

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:23.180
<i>I would've been up against Yukicchi.</i>

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:27.700
<i>I wonder if Sasajima-senpai 
has anyone like that.</i>

00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:33.460
<i>I wonder if my brother did...</i>

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:35.460
President, bad news!

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.000
Sonohara-kun is missing!

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:38.320
What?!

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:40.050
His stuff's gone, too!

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:43.760
There.

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:48.480
I apologize for the wait.

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:51.640
We're still missing a contestant, 
but let's get started anyway.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:54.910
The second group is now entering the fray.

00:22:30.710 --> 00:22:33.540
Welcome, students of Mrs. 
Green Apple High School!

00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:34.980
Hi!

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:38.920
We're here today to present a 
question to the quiz master!

00:22:38.920 --> 00:22:40.920
Oh, really? Let's hear it!

00:22:41.260 --> 00:22:42.880
Here we go! Question!

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:46.840
The "apple" included in the 
name of our high school...

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:48.800
...is from which family of fruit?

00:22:49.120 --> 00:22:50.180
Rosaceae!

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:52.810
Ding ding ding! That's a quiz master for you!

00:22:52.810 --> 00:22:54.490
Yes! I got it right!

00:22:54.490 --> 00:22:57.060
Try asking your friends that 
question tomorrow, everyone!

00:22:57.320 --> 00:22:59.850
And check out "On My Mind"!
